{"assignment_key": "mini-01-bmi-calculator", "title": "Mini Project 1: BMI Calculator", "topic": "Mini Projects", "question": "Build your own BMI (Body Mass Index) calculator.\n\nThe program reads two lines from input:\nLine 1: weight in kilograms (a number, may have decimals)\nLine 2: height in centimeters (a number, may have decimals)\n\nBMI formula: BMI = weight / (height_in_meters * height_in_meters)\n\nPrint EXACTLY two lines:\nYour BMI is: <bmi rounded to 1 decimal place>\nCategory: <category>\n\nCategory rules:\n- BMI < 18.5   -> Underweight\n- 18.5 to 24.9 -> Normal weight\n- 25.0 to 29.9 -> Overweight\n- 30.0 or more -> Obese\n\nExample\nInput:\n70\n175\nOutput:\nYour BMI is: 22.9\nCategory: Normal weight", "starter_code": "# BMI Calculator\n# Read weight (kg) and height (cm), print BMI and category.\nweight = float(input())\n# TODO: read height in cm, compute BMI, print the two required lines\n", "file_name": "main.py", "language": "python", "marks": 10, "is_published": true, "created_by": "83f33ce5-7ca8-4c28-af46-709e3d491285", "tests": [{"input_text": "70\n175\n", "expected_output": "Your BMI is: 22.9\nCategory: Normal weight", "is_hidden": false, "position": 1}, {"input_text": "45\n160\n", "expected_output": "Your BMI is: 17.6\nCategory: Underweight", "is_hidden": false, "position": 2}, {"input_text": "82.5\n170\n", "expected_output": "Your BMI is: 28.5\nCategory: Overweight", "is_hidden": false, "position": 3}, {"input_text": "95\n150\n", "expected_output": "Your BMI is: 42.2\nCategory: Obese", "is_hidden": true, "position": 4}, {"input_text": "61.2\n183.5\n", "expected_output": "Your BMI is: 18.2\nCategory: Underweight", "is_hidden": true, "position": 5}, {"input_text": "68.4\n165.2\n", "expected_output": "Your BMI is: 25.1\nCategory: Overweight", "is_hidden": true, "position": 6}], "batches": ["a81f5ad9-c252-4087-b7ce-75628feb8bf0", "3778803b-1f12-4803-9768-cc0a307742f9"]}
{"assignment_key": "mini-02-interest-calculator", "title": "Mini Project 2: Simple Interest Calculator", "topic": "Mini Projects", "question": "Build a Simple Interest calculator for a small finance shop.\n\nInput (three lines):\nLine 1: principal amount P (a number)\nLine 2: yearly rate of interest R (a number, percent)\nLine 3: time period T in years (a number)\n\nSimple Interest SI = (P * R * T) / 100\nTotal amount = P + SI\n\nPrint EXACTLY two lines:\nSimple Interest: <SI rounded to 2 decimals>\nTotal Amount: <total rounded to 2 decimals>\n\nExample\nInput:\n10000\n7.5\n3\nOutput:\nSimple Interest: 2250.0\nTotal Amount: 12250.0\n\nNote: use round(x, 2) for rounding. If SI has no fraction (like 2250.0) Python\nprints 2250.0 - that exact format is expected.", "starter_code": "# Simple Interest Calculator\nP = float(input())\n# TODO: read R and T, compute SI and total, print both lines\n", "file_name": "main.py", "language": "python", "marks": 10, "is_published": true, "created_by": "83f33ce5-7ca8-4c28-af46-709e3d491285", "tests": [{"input_text": "10000\n7.5\n3\n", "expected_output": "Simple Interest: 2250.0\nTotal Amount: 12250.0", "is_hidden": false, "position": 1}, {"input_text": "5000\n10\n2\n", "expected_output": "Simple Interest: 1000.0\nTotal Amount: 6000.0", "is_hidden": false, "position": 2}, {"input_text": "25000\n8.4\n5\n", "expected_output": "Simple Interest: 10500.0\nTotal Amount: 35500.0", "is_hidden": false, "position": 3}, {"input_text": "1234.5\n6.25\n2.5\n", "expected_output": "Simple Interest: 192.89\nTotal Amount: 1427.39", "is_hidden": true, "position": 4}, {"input_text": "999\n3.3\n1\n", "expected_output": "Simple Interest: 32.97\nTotal Amount: 1031.97", "is_hidden": true, "position": 5}, {"input_text": "100000\n2\n10\n", "expected_output": "Simple Interest: 20000.0\nTotal Amount: 120000.0", "is_hidden": true, "position": 6}], "batches": ["a81f5ad9-c252-4087-b7ce-75628feb8bf0", "3778803b-1f12-4803-9768-cc0a307742f9"]}
{"assignment_key": "mini-03-unit-converter", "title": "Mini Project 3: Unit Converter (km/miles & C/F)", "topic": "Mini Projects", "question": "Build a unit converter that works in two modes.\n\nInput (two lines):\nLine 1: the choice - the number 1 or the number 2\nLine 2: the value to convert (a number, may have decimals)\n\nMode 1: kilometers -> miles.  miles = km * 0.621371\nMode 2: Celsius -> Fahrenheit.  f = (c * 9/5) + 32\n\nPrint EXACTLY one line:\nFor mode 1: <km> km = <miles rounded to 2 decimals> miles\nFor mode 2: <c> degrees Celsius = <f rounded to 1 decimal place> degrees Fahrenheit\n\nPrint the input value as the user typed it (for 5 print 5, for 2.5 print 2.5).\n\nExample\nInput:\n1\n5\nOutput:\n5 km = 3.11 miles\n\nExample\nInput:\n2\n37\nOutput:\n37 degrees Celsius = 98.6 degrees Fahrenheit", "starter_code": "# Unit Converter\nchoice = input()\n# TODO: read the value, convert based on choice, print exactly one line\n", "file_name": "main.py", "language": "python", "marks": 10, "is_published": true, "created_by": "83f33ce5-7ca8-4c28-af46-709e3d491285", "tests": [{"input_text": "1\n5\n", "expected_output": "5 km = 3.11 miles", "is_hidden": false, "position": 1}, {"input_text": "1\n42.195\n", "expected_output": "42.195 km = 26.22 miles", "is_hidden": false, "position": 2}, {"input_text": "2\n37\n", "expected_output": "37 degrees Celsius = 98.6 degrees Fahrenheit", "is_hidden": false, "position": 3}, {"input_text": "2\n100\n", "expected_output": "100 degrees Celsius = 212.0 degrees Fahrenheit", "is_hidden": false, "position": 4}, {"input_text": "1\n0.5\n", "expected_output": "0.5 km = 0.31 miles", "is_hidden": true, "position": 5}, {"input_text": "2\n-40\n", "expected_output": "-40 degrees Celsius = -40.0 degrees Fahrenheit", "is_hidden": true, "position": 6}, {"input_text": "2\n36.6\n", "expected_output": "36.6 degrees Celsius = 97.9 degrees Fahrenheit", "is_hidden": true, "position": 7}], "batches": ["a81f5ad9-c252-4087-b7ce-75628feb8bf0", "3778803b-1f12-4803-9768-cc0a307742f9"]}
{"assignment_key": "mini-04-number-guessing", "title": "Mini Project 4: Number Guessing Game (fixed secret)", "topic": "Mini Projects", "question": "Build a number guessing game. The secret number is read from input so the\ngame can be tested automatically.\n\nInput (two lines):\nLine 1: the secret number (an integer)\nLine 2: space-separated guesses, e.g. 10 50 30 42\n\nThe program must respond to each guess in order:\n- guess < secret  -> print: Too low!\n- guess > secret  -> print: Too high!\n- guess == secret -> print: Correct! You got it in <k> tries!\n  (<k> = number of guesses used so far, counting this one)\n  and STOP reading further guesses.\n\nIf all guesses are used without success print:\nGame over! The number was <secret>\n\nExample\nInput:\n42\n10 50 41 42\nOutput:\nToo low!\nToo high!\nToo low!\nCorrect! You got it in 4 tries!", "starter_code": "# Number Guessing Game\nsecret = int(input())\n# TODO: read the guesses line, process each guess, stop after the correct one\n", "file_name": "main.py", "language": "python", "marks": 10, "is_published": true, "created_by": "83f33ce5-7ca8-4c28-af46-709e3d491285", "tests": [{"input_text": "42\n10 50 41 42\n", "expected_output": "Too low!\nToo high!\nToo low!\nCorrect! You got it in 4 tries!", "is_hidden": false, "position": 1}, {"input_text": "7\n7\n", "expected_output": "Correct! You got it in 1 tries!", "is_hidden": false, "position": 2}, {"input_text": "100\n1 2 3\n", "expected_output": "Too low!\nToo low!\nToo low!\nGame over! The number was 100", "is_hidden": false, "position": 3}, {"input_text": "50\n25 75 50 99\n", "expected_output": "Too low!\nToo high!\nCorrect! You got it in 3 tries!", "is_hidden": true, "position": 4}, {"input_text": "1\n2 3 1\n", "expected_output": "Too high!\nToo high!\nCorrect! You got it in 3 tries!", "is_hidden": true, "position": 5}, {"input_text": "9\n9 9\n", "expected_output": "Correct! You got it in 1 tries!", "is_hidden": true, "position": 6}], "batches": ["a81f5ad9-c252-4087-b7ce-75628feb8bf0", "3778803b-1f12-4803-9768-cc0a307742f9"]}
{"assignment_key": "mini-05-quiz-game", "title": "Mini Project 5: Quiz Game", "topic": "Mini Projects", "question": "Build a small quiz game. The question bank is provided via input.\n\nInput:\nLine 1: N, the number of questions\nThen N lines, each: question|optionA|optionB|optionC|correctLetter\n  (parts separated by the | character; correctLetter is A, B or C)\n\nThe program must print each question with its options, read nothing, then at\nthe end print the score report:\n\nFor each question print exactly:\nQ<i>. <question text>\nA. <optionA>\nB. <optionB>\nC. <optionC>\nAnswer: <correctLetter>\n\nAfter all questions print exactly two lines:\nTotal Questions: <N>\nYour Score: <count of questions whose answer is A>x / <N>\n  wait - no. Score counts how many correct answers are the letter A is NOT\n  required. Simply print the number of questions whose correctLetter is 'A'\n  as \"score\" is wrong. Print instead:\nYour Score: <N> out of <N>\n  i.e. every question is worth 1 point and the full key is shown, so the\n  final line is: Your Score: <N> out of <N>\n\nExample\nInput:\n2\nWhat is 2+2?|3|4|5|B\nCapital of India?|Mumbai|Delhi|Chennai|B\nOutput:\nQ1. What is 2+2?\nA. 3\nB. 4\nC. 5\nAnswer: B\nQ2. Capital of India?\nA. Mumbai\nB. Delhi\nC. Chennai\nAnswer: B\nTotal Questions: 2\nYour Score: 2 out of 2\n\n(The score line always shows the full score because the key is revealed.)", "starter_code": "# Quiz Game\nn = int(input())\n# TODO: read each question line, split on |, print the formatted block\n", "file_name": "main.py", "language": "python", "marks": 10, "is_published": true, "created_by": "83f33ce5-7ca8-4c28-af46-709e3d491285", "tests": [{"input_text": "2\nWhat is 2+2?|3|4|5|B\nCapital of India?|Mumbai|Delhi|Chennai|B\n", "expected_output": "Q1. What is 2+2?\nA. 3\nB. 4\nC. 5\nAnswer: B\nQ2. Capital of India?\nA. Mumbai\nB. Delhi\nC. Chennai\nAnswer: B\nTotal Questions: 2\nYour Score: 2 out of 2", "is_hidden": false, "position": 1}, {"input_text": "1\nSun rises in the?|West|East|North|B\n", "expected_output": "Q1. Sun rises in the?\nA. West\nB. East\nC. North\nAnswer: B\nTotal Questions: 1\nYour Score: 1 out of 1", "is_hidden": false, "position": 2}, {"input_text": "3\n1+1?|1|2|3|B\n5-3?|2|3|4|A\n10/2?|4|5|6|B\n", "expected_output": "Q1. 1+1?\nA. 1\nB. 2\nC. 3\nAnswer: B\nQ2. 5-3?\nA. 2\nB. 3\nC. 4\nAnswer: A\nQ3. 10/2?\nA. 4\nB. 5\nC. 6\nAnswer: B\nTotal Questions: 3\nYour Score: 3 out of 3", "is_hidden": true, "position": 3}, {"input_text": "1\nPython creator?|Guido|Dennis|James|A\n", "expected_output": "Q1. Python creator?\nA. Guido\nB. Dennis\nC. James\nAnswer: A\nTotal Questions: 1\nYour Score: 1 out of 1", "is_hidden": true, "position": 4}], "batches": ["a81f5ad9-c252-4087-b7ce-75628feb8bf0", "3778803b-1f12-4803-9768-cc0a307742f9"]}
{"assignment_key": "mini-06-currency-denominations", "title": "Mini Project 6: Currency Denomination Counter", "topic": "Mini Projects", "question": "An ATM counts the minimum number of notes. Indian denominations available:\n500, 200, 100, 50, 20, 10, 5, 2, 1.\n\nInput: one line with a single integer amount.\nOutput: for every denomination USED (in the order 500,200,100,50,20,10,5,2,1)\nprint exactly:\n<k> x <denomination>\nThen print exactly:\nTotal notes: <total number of notes used>\n\nExample\nInput:\n683\nOutput:\n1 x 500\n1 x 100\n1 x 50\n1 x 20\n1 x 10\n1 x 2\n1 x 1\nTotal notes: 7\n\nExample\nInput:\n400\nOutput:\n2 x 200\nTotal notes: 2", "starter_code": "# Currency Denomination Counter\namount = int(input())\n# TODO: greedy counting from 500 down to 1, print each used denomination\n", "file_name": "main.py", "language": "python", "marks": 10, "is_published": true, "created_by": "83f33ce5-7ca8-4c28-af46-709e3d491285", "tests": [{"input_text": "683\n", "expected_output": "1 x 500\n1 x 100\n1 x 50\n1 x 20\n1 x 10\n1 x 2\n1 x 1\nTotal notes: 7", "is_hidden": false, "position": 1}, {"input_text": "400\n", "expected_output": "2 x 200\nTotal notes: 2", "is_hidden": false, "position": 2}, {"input_text": "1\n", "expected_output": "1 x 1\nTotal notes: 1", "is_hidden": false, "position": 3}, {"input_text": "2889\n", "expected_output": "5 x 500\n1 x 200\n1 x 100\n1 x 50\n1 x 20\n1 x 10\n1 x 5\n2 x 2\nTotal notes: 13", "is_hidden": true, "position": 4}, {"input_text": "77\n", "expected_output": "1 x 50\n1 x 20\n1 x 5\n1 x 2\nTotal notes: 4", "is_hidden": true, "position": 5}, {"input_text": "500\n", "expected_output": "1 x 500\nTotal notes: 1", "is_hidden": true, "position": 6}], "batches": ["a81f5ad9-c252-4087-b7ce-75628feb8bf0", "3778803b-1f12-4803-9768-cc0a307742f9"]}
{"assignment_key": "mini-07-password-strength", "title": "Mini Project 7: Password Strength Checker", "topic": "Mini Projects", "question": "Build a password strength checker.\n\nInput: one line containing the password (it may contain spaces - read the\nwhole line; a password made only of spaces is not tested).\n\nRules (checked in this order, first match wins):\n- length < 6                                        -> print: Weak\n- length >= 6 AND length <= 10                      -> print: Medium\n- length > 10 AND has digit AND has uppercase       -> print: Strong\n- length > 10 (otherwise)                           -> print: Medium\n\nExample\nInput:\nabc\nOutput:\nWeak\nExample\nInput:\nhello world\nOutput:\nMedium\nExample\nInput:\nHelloWorld123\nOutput:\nStrong", "starter_code": "# Password Strength Checker\npassword = input()\n# TODO: apply the rules in order and print exactly one word\n", "file_name": "main.py", "language": "python", "marks": 10, "is_published": true, "created_by": "83f33ce5-7ca8-4c28-af46-709e3d491285", "tests": [{"input_text": "abc\n", "expected_output": "Weak", "is_hidden": false, "position": 1}, {"input_text": "hello world\n", "expected_output": "Medium", "is_hidden": false, "position": 2}, {"input_text": "HelloWorld123\n", "expected_output": "Strong", "is_hidden": false, "position": 3}, {"input_text": "abcdef\n", "expected_output": "Medium", "is_hidden": true, "position": 4}, {"input_text": "12345\n", "expected_output": "Weak", "is_hidden": true, "position": 5}, {"input_text": "this is a long password\n", "expected_output": "Medium", "is_hidden": true, "position": 6}, {"input_text": "Abcdefghij12345\n", "expected_output": "Strong", "is_hidden": true, "position": 7}], "batches": ["a81f5ad9-c252-4087-b7ce-75628feb8bf0", "3778803b-1f12-4803-9768-cc0a307742f9"]}
{"assignment_key": "mini-08-electricity-bill", "title": "Mini Project 8: Electricity Bill Calculator", "topic": "Mini Projects", "question": "Build an electricity bill calculator with slab rates.\n\nInput: one line, units consumed (an integer).\nSlab rates (charged progressively, like income tax slabs):\n- first 100 units: 3.50 per unit\n- next 100 units (101-200): 4.50 per unit\n- above 200 units: 6.00 per unit\nFixed meter charge is always added: 50.00\n\nPrint EXACTLY one line:\nBill: <amount rounded to 2 decimals>\n\nExample (150 units -> 100*3.50 + 50*4.50 + 50 fixed)\nInput:\n150\nOutput:\nBill: 625.0\n\nExample\nInput:\n250\nOutput:\nBill: 1150.0\n\nNote: round(x, 2) prints 725.0 for 725.00 - that exact format is expected.", "starter_code": "# Electricity Bill Calculator\nunits = int(input())\n# TODO: compute slab bill + 50 meter charge, print 'Bill: <x>'\n", "file_name": "main.py", "language": "python", "marks": 10, "is_published": true, "created_by": "83f33ce5-7ca8-4c28-af46-709e3d491285", "tests": [{"input_text": "150\n", "expected_output": "Bill: 625.0", "is_hidden": false, "position": 1}, {"input_text": "250\n", "expected_output": "Bill: 1150.0", "is_hidden": false, "position": 2}, {"input_text": "50\n", "expected_output": "Bill: 225.0", "is_hidden": false, "position": 3}, {"input_text": "0\n", "expected_output": "Bill: 50.0", "is_hidden": false, "position": 4}, {"input_text": "100\n", "expected_output": "Bill: 400.0", "is_hidden": false, "position": 5}, {"input_text": "201\n", "expected_output": "Bill: 856.0", "is_hidden": true, "position": 6}, {"input_text": "500\n", "expected_output": "Bill: 2650.0", "is_hidden": true, "position": 7}, {"input_text": "175\n", "expected_output": "Bill: 737.5", "is_hidden": true, "position": 8}], "batches": ["a81f5ad9-c252-4087-b7ce-75628feb8bf0", "3778803b-1f12-4803-9768-cc0a307742f9"]}
{"assignment_key": "mini-09-temperature-analyzer", "title": "Mini Project 9: Temperature Analyzer", "topic": "Mini Projects", "question": "Build a weather-log analyzer.\n\nInput (two lines):\nLine 1: N, how many temperature readings follow (integer, N >= 1)\nLine 2: N readings separated by spaces (integers, Celsius)\n\nPrint EXACTLY four lines:\nHighest: <max reading>\nLowest: <min reading>\nAverage: <average rounded to 2 decimals>\nAbove Average Days: <how many readings are strictly greater than the average>\n\nExample\nInput:\n5\n30 32 28 35 31\nOutput:\nHighest: 35\nLowest: 28\nAverage: 31.2\nAbove Average Days: 2", "starter_code": "# Temperature Analyzer\nn = int(input())\n# TODO: read the readings line, compute max, min, average, above-average count\n", "file_name": "main.py", "language": "python", "marks": 10, "is_published": true, "created_by": "83f33ce5-7ca8-4c28-af46-709e3d491285", "tests": [{"input_text": "5\n30 32 28 35 31\n", "expected_output": "Highest: 35\nLowest: 28\nAverage: 31.2\nAbove Average Days: 2", "is_hidden": false, "position": 1}, {"input_text": "1\n25\n", "expected_output": "Highest: 25\nLowest: 25\nAverage: 25.0\nAbove Average Days: 0", "is_hidden": false, "position": 2}, {"input_text": "4\n10 20 30 40\n", "expected_output": "Highest: 40\nLowest: 10\nAverage: 25.0\nAbove Average Days: 2", "is_hidden": false, "position": 3}, {"input_text": "6\n-5 0 5 -10 8 4\n", "expected_output": "Highest: 8\nLowest: -10\nAverage: 0.33\nAbove Average Days: 3", "is_hidden": true, "position": 4}, {"input_text": "3\n7 7 7\n", "expected_output": "Highest: 7\nLowest: 7\nAverage: 7.0\nAbove Average Days: 0", "is_hidden": true, "position": 5}, {"input_text": "7\n12 14 16 18 20 22 24\n", "expected_output": "Highest: 24\nLowest: 12\nAverage: 18.0\nAbove Average Days: 3", "is_hidden": true, "position": 6}], "batches": ["a81f5ad9-c252-4087-b7ce-75628feb8bf0", "3778803b-1f12-4803-9768-cc0a307742f9"]}
{"assignment_key": "mini-10-word-counter", "title": "Mini Project 10: Word Counter & Analyzer", "topic": "Mini Projects", "question": "Build a text analyzer for a single sentence.\n\nInput: one line of text (may contain spaces; NOT empty).\n\nPrint EXACTLY five lines:\nWords: <number of words>\nCharacters: <total characters including spaces>\nCharacters without spaces: <total minus space characters>\nLongest Word: <longest word; if tie, the first occurring one>\nUppercase Count: <number of uppercase letters>\n\nExample\nInput:\nI love Python programming\nOutput:\nWords: 4\nCharacters: 25\nCharacters without spaces: 22\nLongest Word: programming\nUppercase Count: 2", "starter_code": "# Word Counter\nsentence = input()\n# TODO: split into words and print the five required lines\n", "file_name": "main.py", "language": "python", "marks": 10, "is_published": true, "created_by": "83f33ce5-7ca8-4c28-af46-709e3d491285", "tests": [{"input_text": "I love Python programming\n", "expected_output": "Words: 4\nCharacters: 25\nCharacters without spaces: 22\nLongest Word: programming\nUppercase Count: 2", "is_hidden": false, "position": 1}, {"input_text": "hello\n", "expected_output": "Words: 1\nCharacters: 5\nCharacters without spaces: 5\nLongest Word: hello\nUppercase Count: 0", "is_hidden": false, "position": 2}, {"input_text": "A B AB\n", "expected_output": "Words: 3\nCharacters: 6\nCharacters without spaces: 4\nLongest Word: AB\nUppercase Count: 4", "is_hidden": true, "position": 3}, {"input_text": "Kaveri Academy teaches Python\n", "expected_output": "Words: 4\nCharacters: 29\nCharacters without spaces: 26\nLongest Word: Academy\nUppercase Count: 3", "is_hidden": true, "position": 4}, {"input_text": "aBcD eFgH\n", "expected_output": "Words: 2\nCharacters: 9\nCharacters without spaces: 8\nLongest Word: aBcD\nUppercase Count: 4", "is_hidden": true, "position": 5}], "batches": ["a81f5ad9-c252-4087-b7ce-75628feb8bf0", "3778803b-1f12-4803-9768-cc0a307742f9"]}
{"assignment_key": "mini-11-expense-tracker", "title": "Mini Project 11: Expense Tracker", "topic": "Mini Projects", "question": "Build a mini expense tracker.\n\nInput:\nLine 1: N, the number of expenses\nThen N lines, each: <category> <amount>   (single space separator,\namount is a number; categories are single words like food, travel)\n\nPrint EXACTLY:\nTotal Spent: <sum of all amounts rounded to 2>\nHighest: <category with the highest total amount>\n  (if tie on total, the category that reached its total first in input order\n   wins - simple approach: first category in input order with max total)\nAverage: <total / N rounded to 2>\n\nExample\nInput:\n4\nfood 250\ntravel 100\nfood 50\ntravel 200\nOutput:\nTotal Spent: 600.0\nHighest: food\nAverage: 150.0", "starter_code": "# Expense Tracker\nn = int(input())\n# TODO: read each 'category amount' line and report totals\n", "file_name": "main.py", "language": "python", "marks": 10, "is_published": true, "created_by": "83f33ce5-7ca8-4c28-af46-709e3d491285", "tests": [{"input_text": "4\nfood 250\ntravel 100\nfood 50\ntravel 200\n", "expected_output": "Total Spent: 600.0\nHighest: food\nAverage: 150.0", "is_hidden": false, "position": 1}, {"input_text": "1\nbooks 499.5\n", "expected_output": "Total Spent: 499.5\nHighest: books\nAverage: 499.5", "is_hidden": false, "position": 2}, {"input_text": "3\na 10\nb 10\nc 10\n", "expected_output": "Total Spent: 30.0\nHighest: a\nAverage: 10.0", "is_hidden": false, "position": 3}, {"input_text": "5\nx 1.25\ny 2.5\nx 0.75\ny 2.5\nz 3\n", "expected_output": "Total Spent: 10.0\nHighest: y\nAverage: 2.0", "is_hidden": true, "position": 4}, {"input_text": "2\nsnacks 45\nmovies 300\n", "expected_output": "Total Spent: 345.0\nHighest: movies\nAverage: 172.5", "is_hidden": true, "position": 5}], "batches": ["a81f5ad9-c252-4087-b7ce-75628feb8bf0", "3778803b-1f12-4803-9768-cc0a307742f9"]}
{"assignment_key": "mini-12-todo-app", "title": "Mini Project 12: Todo App (console)", "topic": "Mini Projects", "question": "Build your own console Todo app. The tasks and commands are provided via\ninput so the app can be tested automatically.\n\nInput:\nLine 1: N, number of initial tasks\nThen N lines, each an initial task title (single line text)\nThen one line: M, number of commands\nThen M lines, each a command:\n  done <task number>   -> mark that task done (task numbers start at 1,\n                          based on position in the CURRENT list)\n  remove <task number> -> delete that task from the list\n  (any other command lines are ignored)\n\nOutput: print the final list state, one line per remaining task, in order:\n[<status>] <title>\nwhere <status> is DONE or TODO.\nIf no tasks remain print exactly: No tasks\n\nExample\nInput:\n3\nBuy milk\nStudy Python\nCall friend\n3\ndone 1\nremove 2\ndone 2\nOutput:\n[DONE] Buy milk\n[DONE] Call friend\n\nExplanation: after 'done 1' task 1 is DONE; 'remove 2' deletes 'Study\nPython'; the list is now [Buy milk(DONE), Call friend(TODO)]; 'done 2'\nmarks Call friend DONE.", "starter_code": "# Todo App\ntasks = []\nn = int(input())\n# TODO: read tasks, then commands, then print the final state\n", "file_name": "main.py", "language": "python", "marks": 10, "is_published": true, "created_by": "83f33ce5-7ca8-4c28-af46-709e3d491285", "tests": [{"input_text": "3\nBuy milk\nStudy Python\nCall friend\n3\ndone 1\nremove 2\ndone 2\n", "expected_output": "[DONE] Buy milk\n[DONE] Call friend", "is_hidden": false, "position": 1}, {"input_text": "1\nOnly task\n1\nremove 1\n", "expected_output": "No tasks", "is_hidden": false, "position": 2}, {"input_text": "2\nA\nB\n0\n", "expected_output": "[TODO] A\n[TODO] B", "is_hidden": false, "position": 3}, {"input_text": "4\nT1\nT2\nT3\nT4\n4\ndone 4\nremove 1\ndone 1\ndone 2\n", "expected_output": "[DONE] T2\n[DONE] T3\n[DONE] T4", "is_hidden": true, "position": 4}, {"input_text": "2\nX\nY\n2\nremove 5\ndone 0\n", "expected_output": "[TODO] X\n[TODO] Y", "is_hidden": true, "position": 5}, {"input_text": "0\n1\ndone 1\n", "expected_output": "No tasks", "is_hidden": true, "position": 6}], "batches": ["a81f5ad9-c252-4087-b7ce-75628feb8bf0", "3778803b-1f12-4803-9768-cc0a307742f9"]}
{"assignment_key": "mini-13-contact-book", "title": "Mini Project 13: Contact Book", "topic": "Mini Projects", "question": "Build a Contact Book with a dictionary.\n\nInput:\nLine 1: N, number of saved contacts\nThen N lines, each: <name> <10-digit phone number>  (single space)\nThen one line: Q, number of lookups\nThen Q lines, each: a name to search (exact match)\n\nFor each lookup print exactly:\n<name>: <phone>\nor, when not found:\n<name>: Not found\n\nExample\nInput:\n2\nAnil 9876543210\nPriya 9123456780\n3\nAnil\nRavi\nPriya\nOutput:\nAnil: 9876543210\nRavi: Not found\nPriya: 9123456780", "starter_code": "# Contact Book\ncontacts = {}\nn = int(input())\n# TODO: save contacts, then answer lookups\n", "file_name": "main.py", "language": "python", "marks": 10, "is_published": true, "created_by": "83f33ce5-7ca8-4c28-af46-709e3d491285", "tests": [{"input_text": "2\nAnil 9876543210\nPriya 9123456780\n3\nAnil\nRavi\nPriya\n", "expected_output": "Anil: 9876543210\nRavi: Not found\nPriya: 9123456780", "is_hidden": false, "position": 1}, {"input_text": "1\nSolo 9000000000\n2\nSolo\nsolo\n", "expected_output": "Solo: 9000000000\nsolo: Not found", "is_hidden": false, "position": 2}, {"input_text": "0\n1\nNobody\n", "expected_output": "Nobody: Not found", "is_hidden": false, "position": 3}, {"input_text": "3\nB 1111111111\nA 2222222222\nC 3333333333\n3\nC\nA\nB\n", "expected_output": "C: 3333333333\nA: 2222222222\nB: 1111111111", "is_hidden": true, "position": 4}, {"input_text": "1\nKiran 1234567890\n0\n", "expected_output": "", "is_hidden": true, "position": 5}], "batches": ["a81f5ad9-c252-4087-b7ce-75628feb8bf0", "3778803b-1f12-4803-9768-cc0a307742f9"]}
{"assignment_key": "mini-14-rock-paper-scissors", "title": "Mini Project 14: Rock Paper Scissors (fixed computer)", "topic": "Mini Projects", "question": "Play Rock-Paper-Scissors against a computer whose moves are given in the\ninput (so the game is deterministic and testable).\n\nInput (two lines):\nLine 1: the computer's moves, space-separated words from rock/paper/scissors\nLine 2: the player's moves, space-separated words from rock/paper/scissors\n(both lines have the same count of moves)\n\nRules: rock beats scissors, paper beats rock, scissors beats paper,\nsame move is a tie.\n\nScore: win = 1 point for the winner, tie = 1 point for each? NO - keep it\nsimple: each round the winner gets 1 point, a tie gives nobody a point.\n\nPrint EXACTLY three lines:\nPlayer: <player points>\nComputer: <computer points>\nResult: <You win!|Computer wins!|It's a tie!>\n(the Result line compares total points; equal points -> It's a tie!)\n\nExample\nInput:\nrock paper scissors\npaper scissors rock\nOutput:\nPlayer: 3\nComputer: 0\nResult: You win!", "starter_code": "# Rock Paper Scissors\ncomputer_moves = input().split()\n# TODO: read player moves, score each round, print the result\n", "file_name": "main.py", "language": "python", "marks": 10, "is_published": true, "created_by": "83f33ce5-7ca8-4c28-af46-709e3d491285", "tests": [{"input_text": "rock paper scissors\npaper scissors rock\n", "expected_output": "Player: 3\nComputer: 0\nResult: You win!", "is_hidden": false, "position": 1}, {"input_text": "rock rock rock\nscissors paper rock\n", "expected_output": "Player: 1\nComputer: 1\nResult: It's a tie!", "is_hidden": false, "position": 2}, {"input_text": "paper\nscissors\n", "expected_output": "Player: 1\nComputer: 0\nResult: You win!", "is_hidden": false, "position": 3}, {"input_text": "rock paper\nrock paper\n", "expected_output": "Player: 0\nComputer: 0\nResult: It's a tie!", "is_hidden": true, "position": 4}, {"input_text": "scissors scissors scissors\nrock paper scissors\n", "expected_output": "Player: 1\nComputer: 1\nResult: It's a tie!", "is_hidden": true, "position": 5}, {"input_text": "rock\npaper\n", "expected_output": "Player: 1\nComputer: 0\nResult: You win!", "is_hidden": true, "position": 6}], "batches": ["a81f5ad9-c252-4087-b7ce-75628feb8bf0", "3778803b-1f12-4803-9768-cc0a307742f9"]}
{"assignment_key": "mini-15-palindrome-tool", "title": "Mini Project 15: Palindrome Checker", "topic": "Mini Projects", "question": "Build a palindrome checker for sentences.\n\nInput:\nLine 1: N, the number of sentences\nThen N lines, each a sentence (letters, digits and spaces; case must be\nignored; spaces must be ignored; punctuation is not tested)\n\nFor each sentence print exactly one line:\nYes\nor\nNo\n\nA sentence is a palindrome when it reads the same forwards and backwards\nafter ignoring case and spaces.\n\nExample\nInput:\n3\nNever odd or even\nHello\nA man a plan a canal Panama\nOutput:\nYes\nNo\nYes", "starter_code": "# Palindrome Checker\nn = int(input())\n# TODO: for each sentence, ignore case+spaces and check the palindrome\n", "file_name": "main.py", "language": "python", "marks": 10, "is_published": true, "created_by": "83f33ce5-7ca8-4c28-af46-709e3d491285", "tests": [{"input_text": "3\nNever odd or even\nHello\nA man a plan a canal Panama\n", "expected_output": "Yes\nNo\nYes", "is_hidden": false, "position": 1}, {"input_text": "1\nracecar\n", "expected_output": "Yes", "is_hidden": false, "position": 2}, {"input_text": "2\nPython\nmadam\n", "expected_output": "No\nYes", "is_hidden": false, "position": 3}, {"input_text": "2\nWas it a car or a cat I saw\nKaveri\n", "expected_output": "Yes\nNo", "is_hidden": true, "position": 4}, {"input_text": "1\na\n", "expected_output": "Yes", "is_hidden": true, "position": 5}, {"input_text": "1\nAb ba\n", "expected_output": "Yes", "is_hidden": true, "position": 6}], "batches": ["a81f5ad9-c252-4087-b7ce-75628feb8bf0", "3778803b-1f12-4803-9768-cc0a307742f9"]}
{"assignment_key": "mini-16-times-table", "title": "Mini Project 16: Multiplication Table Generator", "topic": "Mini Projects", "question": "Build a multiplication table generator.\n\nInput: one line with the number N (integer 1..20).\n\nPrint the table of N from 1 to 10, EXACTLY in this format:\nN x 1 = N1\nN x 2 = N2\n...\nN x 10 = N10\n(where N is the number and Nx is the product)\n\nExample\nInput:\n7\nOutput:\n7 x 1 = 7\n7 x 2 = 14\n7 x 3 = 21\n7 x 4 = 28\n7 x 5 = 35\n7 x 6 = 42\n7 x 7 = 49\n7 x 8 = 56\n7 x 9 = 63\n7 x 10 = 70", "starter_code": "# Multiplication Table\nn = int(input())\n# TODO: print the table from 1 to 10\n", "file_name": "main.py", "language": "python", "marks": 10, "is_published": true, "created_by": "83f33ce5-7ca8-4c28-af46-709e3d491285", "tests": [{"input_text": "7\n", "expected_output": "7 x 1 = 7\n7 x 2 = 14\n7 x 3 = 21\n7 x 4 = 28\n7 x 5 = 35\n7 x 6 = 42\n7 x 7 = 49\n7 x 8 = 56\n7 x 9 = 63\n7 x 10 = 70", "is_hidden": false, "position": 1}, {"input_text": "1\n", "expected_output": "1 x 1 = 1\n1 x 2 = 2\n1 x 3 = 3\n1 x 4 = 4\n1 x 5 = 5\n1 x 6 = 6\n1 x 7 = 7\n1 x 8 = 8\n1 x 9 = 9\n1 x 10 = 10", "is_hidden": false, "position": 2}, {"input_text": "12\n", "expected_output": "12 x 1 = 12\n12 x 2 = 24\n12 x 3 = 36\n12 x 4 = 48\n12 x 5 = 60\n12 x 6 = 72\n12 x 7 = 84\n12 x 8 = 96\n12 x 9 = 108\n12 x 10 = 120", "is_hidden": true, "position": 3}, {"input_text": "20\n", "expected_output": "20 x 1 = 20\n20 x 2 = 40\n20 x 3 = 60\n20 x 4 = 80\n20 x 5 = 100\n20 x 6 = 120\n20 x 7 = 140\n20 x 8 = 160\n20 x 9 = 180\n20 x 10 = 200", "is_hidden": true, "position": 4}], "batches": ["a81f5ad9-c252-4087-b7ce-75628feb8bf0", "3778803b-1f12-4803-9768-cc0a307742f9"]}
{"assignment_key": "mini-17-grade-manager", "title": "Mini Project 17: Student Grade Manager", "topic": "Mini Projects", "question": "Build a grade manager for one class.\n\nInput:\nLine 1: N students\nThen N lines: <name> <marks>   (marks is an integer 0..100)\n\nFor each student print exactly one line:\n<name>: <grade>\nGrade rules:\nmarks >= 90 -> A+\nmarks >= 75 -> A\nmarks >= 60 -> B\nmarks >= 40 -> C\nmarks <  40 -> F\n\nThen print exactly two class summary lines:\nClass Average: <average of marks rounded to 1 decimal>\nTopper: <name of the student with the highest marks (first on tie)>\n\nExample\nInput:\n3\nAnil 92\nPriya 68\nRavi 45\nOutput:\nAnil: A+\nPriya: B\nRavi: C\nClass Average: 68.3\nTopper: Anil", "starter_code": "# Grade Manager\nn = int(input())\n# TODO: read name+marks, print grades, then the class summary\n", "file_name": "main.py", "language": "python", "marks": 10, "is_published": true, "created_by": "83f33ce5-7ca8-4c28-af46-709e3d491285", "tests": [{"input_text": "3\nAnil 92\nPriya 68\nRavi 45\n", "expected_output": "Anil: A+\nPriya: B\nRavi: C\nClass Average: 68.3\nTopper: Anil", "is_hidden": false, "position": 1}, {"input_text": "2\nA 100\nB 0\n", "expected_output": "A: A+\nB: F\nClass Average: 50.0\nTopper: A", "is_hidden": false, "position": 2}, {"input_text": "1\nSolo 75\n", "expected_output": "Solo: A\nClass Average: 75.0\nTopper: Solo", "is_hidden": false, "position": 3}, {"input_text": "4\nX 39\nY 40\nZ 89\nW 90\n", "expected_output": "X: F\nY: C\nZ: A\nW: A+\nClass Average: 64.5\nTopper: W", "is_hidden": true, "position": 4}, {"input_text": "2\nB 50\nA 50\n", "expected_output": "B: C\nA: C\nClass Average: 50.0\nTopper: B", "is_hidden": true, "position": 5}, {"input_text": "3\nP 60\nQ 60\nR 60\n", "expected_output": "P: B\nQ: B\nR: B\nClass Average: 60.0\nTopper: P", "is_hidden": true, "position": 6}], "batches": ["a81f5ad9-c252-4087-b7ce-75628feb8bf0", "3778803b-1f12-4803-9768-cc0a307742f9"]}
{"assignment_key": "mini-18-bank-account", "title": "Mini Project 18: Bank Account Simulator", "topic": "Mini Projects", "question": "Simulate a bank account. Start with balance 0. Process a list of\noperations in order.\n\nInput:\nLine 1: N operations\nThen N lines, each one of:\n  deposit <amount>\n  withdraw <amount>\n  balance\nRules: a withdrawal is allowed only if the balance stays >= 0 after it;\notherwise print exactly: Insufficient balance\nPrint exactly one line per operation, in order:\n  deposit -> Deposited <amount>. Balance: <balance>\n  withdraw -> Withdrew <amount>. Balance: <balance>\n  balance -> Balance: <balance>\nAmounts are integers. Print the balance as an integer (no decimals).\n\nExample\nInput:\n5\ndeposit 1000\nwithdraw 400\nbalance\nwithdraw 700\nbalance\nOutput:\nDeposited 1000. Balance: 1000\nWithdrew 400. Balance: 600\nBalance: 600\nInsufficient balance\nBalance: 600", "starter_code": "# Bank Account Simulator\nbalance = 0\nn = int(input())\n# TODO: process deposits, withdrawals and balance queries in order\n", "file_name": "main.py", "language": "python", "marks": 10, "is_published": true, "created_by": "83f33ce5-7ca8-4c28-af46-709e3d491285", "tests": [{"input_text": "5\ndeposit 1000\nwithdraw 400\nbalance\nwithdraw 700\nbalance\n", "expected_output": "Deposited 1000. Balance: 1000\nWithdrew 400. Balance: 600\nBalance: 600\nInsufficient balance\nBalance: 600", "is_hidden": false, "position": 1}, {"input_text": "3\ndeposit 500\nwithdraw 500\nbalance\n", "expected_output": "Deposited 500. Balance: 500\nWithdrew 500. Balance: 0\nBalance: 0", "is_hidden": false, "position": 2}, {"input_text": "1\nbalance\n", "expected_output": "Balance: 0", "is_hidden": false, "position": 3}, {"input_text": "4\ndeposit 100\nwithdraw 1\nwithdraw 99\nbalance\n", "expected_output": "Deposited 100. Balance: 100\nWithdrew 1. Balance: 99\nWithdrew 99. Balance: 0\nBalance: 0", "is_hidden": true, "position": 4}, {"input_text": "2\nwithdraw 1\nbalance\n", "expected_output": "Insufficient balance\nBalance: 0", "is_hidden": true, "position": 5}, {"input_text": "3\ndeposit 250\ndeposit 250\nbalance\n", "expected_output": "Deposited 250. Balance: 250\nDeposited 250. Balance: 500\nBalance: 500", "is_hidden": true, "position": 6}], "batches": ["a81f5ad9-c252-4087-b7ce-75628feb8bf0", "3778803b-1f12-4803-9768-cc0a307742f9"]}
{"assignment_key": "mini-19-library-fine", "title": "Mini Project 19: Library Fine Calculator", "topic": "Mini Projects", "question": "A library charges fines progressively:\n- first 5 days late: 2 rupees per day\n- next 5 days (6-10): 5 rupees per day\n- after 10 days: 10 rupees per day\nReturning on time (0 days late) has no fine.\n\nInput: one line, days late (integer >= 0).\n\nPrint EXACTLY one line:\nFine: <total fine in rupees>\n\nExamples\nInput:\n3\nOutput:\nFine: 6\nInput:\n8\nOutput:\nFine: 25        (5*2 + 3*5)\nInput:\n0\nOutput:\nFine: 0", "starter_code": "# Library Fine Calculator\ndays = int(input())\n# TODO: compute the progressive fine\n", "file_name": "main.py", "language": "python", "marks": 10, "is_published": true, "created_by": "83f33ce5-7ca8-4c28-af46-709e3d491285", "tests": [{"input_text": "3\n", "expected_output": "Fine: 6", "is_hidden": false, "position": 1}, {"input_text": "8\n", "expected_output": "Fine: 25", "is_hidden": false, "position": 2}, {"input_text": "0\n", "expected_output": "Fine: 0", "is_hidden": false, "position": 3}, {"input_text": "5\n", "expected_output": "Fine: 10", "is_hidden": false, "position": 4}, {"input_text": "10\n", "expected_output": "Fine: 35", "is_hidden": false, "position": 5}, {"input_text": "15\n", "expected_output": "Fine: 85", "is_hidden": true, "position": 6}, {"input_text": "11\n", "expected_output": "Fine: 45", "is_hidden": true, "position": 7}, {"input_text": "1\n", "expected_output": "Fine: 2", "is_hidden": true, "position": 8}], "batches": ["a81f5ad9-c252-4087-b7ce-75628feb8bf0", "3778803b-1f12-4803-9768-cc0a307742f9"]}
{"assignment_key": "mini-20-tic-tac-toe", "title": "Mini Project 20: Tic-Tac-Toe Winner Checker", "topic": "Mini Projects", "question": "Read a finished tic-tac-toe board and report the result.\n\nInput: 3 lines, each with 3 characters separated by spaces.\nEach character is X, O or - (dash = empty).\n\nPrint EXACTLY one line:\n- X wins      (if X has three in a row)\n- O wins      (if O has three in a row)\n- Draw        (otherwise)\nA win is any full row, column or diagonal of the same non-empty symbol.\nThe tests never contain both players winning at once.\n\nExample\nInput:\nX O X\nO X O\nO X X\nOutput:\nX wins\n\n(X has the main diagonal positions 1,5,9.)\n\nExample\nInput:\nX O X\nX O O\nO X X\nOutput:\nDraw", "starter_code": "# Tic-Tac-Toe Winner Checker\nboard = []\nfor _ in range(3):\n    board.append(input().split())\n# TODO: check rows, columns and diagonals, print the result\n", "file_name": "main.py", "language": "python", "marks": 10, "is_published": true, "created_by": "83f33ce5-7ca8-4c28-af46-709e3d491285", "tests": [{"input_text": "X O X\nO X O\nO X X\n", "expected_output": "X wins", "is_hidden": false, "position": 1}, {"input_text": "X O X\nX O O\nO X X\n", "expected_output": "Draw", "is_hidden": false, "position": 2}, {"input_text": "O O X\nO X X\nX - -\n", "expected_output": "X wins", "is_hidden": false, "position": 3}, {"input_text": "X X O\nX O -\nO - -\n", "expected_output": "O wins", "is_hidden": true, "position": 4}, {"input_text": "X X X\nO O -\n- - -\n", "expected_output": "X wins", "is_hidden": true, "position": 5}, {"input_text": "X O X\nO X O\nX O X\n", "expected_output": "X wins", "is_hidden": true, "position": 6}, {"input_text": "O - O\n- X -\nO - X\n", "expected_output": "Draw", "is_hidden": true, "position": 7}], "batches": ["a81f5ad9-c252-4087-b7ce-75628feb8bf0", "3778803b-1f12-4803-9768-cc0a307742f9"]}
